# Deny by default, then re-include only the skills that are shared.
#
# Two rules make this work, and breaking either one silently breaks the file:
#
#  1. Exclude a directory's CONTENTS (`/skills/*`), never the directory itself
#     (`/skills/`). Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so nothing
#     beneath one can ever be re-included by a later `!` line.
#  2. Last matching pattern wins. The hygiene section at the bottom therefore
#     still applies inside re-included skill directories.
#
# `/skills/*` matches direct children only, dotfiles included, so an agent CLI's
# own system-skill directory stays out without needing its own rule. Everything
# nested inside a re-included skill is tracked normally.
#
# To share a new skill: add one `!/skills/<name>/` line below, keeping the list
# alphabetical, then `git add skills/<name>`.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/bin/
!/skills/
/skills/*

!/skills/codex-migrate-session/
!/skills/handoff/
!/skills/history-audit/
!/skills/init-repo/
!/skills/never-commit/
!/skills/plan-upfront/
!/skills/tmux-message/
!/skills/token-cost/
!/skills/wsl-service/

# Hygiene, applied at every depth including inside shared skills. Skills may
# ship scripts, so build and cache artefacts of their languages belong here.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/*.local.*
CLAUDE.local.md
.codex/worktrees/
**/do_not_commit/
